    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d186">

                <pb facs="0188" n="176" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg176"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.00/12–2844: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacVeagh</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Athens</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-28T16:00:00+02:00">December 28,
                            1944—4 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 29—9:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>194. I desire to thank the Department for the information conveyed in its No. 151
                    of December 27, 1 p.m.<anchor n="75" xml:id="d186-f1"/> just received. Mr.
                    Churchill has left Athens, and I greatly regret that my long conversation with
                    him yesterday (see my 190, of December 27, 7 p.m. for the President) had to be
                    carried on without my knowledge of this important background.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVeagh</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d186-f1" n="75" xml:id="d186-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it informed Ambassador MacVeagh of President Roosevelt’s telegram
                    No. 673, December 13, to Prime Minister Churchill, <ref target="#pg150">p.
                        150</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
